<!--
  Commander Battle's Sturgian troop classes, merged into Native's mpclassdivisions.xml (MPClassDivisions, MultiplayerGame
  only). Same rules as cb_mpclassdivisions_vlandia.xml:
  - One class per weight of a formation class (role): infantry heavy/medium/light, ranged light/heavy, cavalry
    light/heavy. The weight label comes from the multiplier bands per role (CommanderRoles.WeightBands).
  - Sturgia has exactly 7 classes, so all of them take over the 7 stock class ids in place (_replaceWhileMerging="true")
    and keep the stock index (MissionPeer.SelectedTroopIndex). No new class ids: never put _replaceWhileMerging on a NEW
    id (with no id match the merger replaces the FIRST class of the file instead, MBObjectManager.MergeElements).
  - A stock id's role comes only from its hero's default_group, so mp_skirmisher_sturgia becomes the heavy archers
    (the nearest meaning left once the infantry and cavalry ids are taken).
  - multiplier: the class's size weight. A formation fields budget x ceil(100 x multiplier) / the average of its role's
    classes, so it only compares within a role.
  - The only perk list (perk_list="1") is the weapon setups. Index 0 is the class's own loadout; the others swap weapon
    slots with AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn (target Any: commander and troops). No TroopCountOnSpawn: only the weight sets
    the count. game_mode="all": the server's GameType is CommanderBattle, so stock "Captain" perks would never apply.
  - Setup order is the AI order (MissionMultiplayerCommanderBattle.AssignDefaultClasses): the k-th AI formation of a
    role fields setup k. Index 0 is Sturgia's signature setup.
  - Culture variance pass (docs/plans/troop-types.md): Sturgia is the shield-wall culture. The biggest round shields
    with the most hit points, the heaviest infantry armour and the slowest infantry; two-handed axe berserkers; cavalry
    with big round shields and two-handed maces. Weak ranged (Sturgia's own weaker bows: Nordic shortbow for the levy,
    hunting longbow for the veterans, plain bodkin arrows), no pikes or great spears, no skirmishers, no throwing
    weapons, no mounted crossbowmen.
    Infantry: spear + big round shield, axe + big round shield, two-handed axe. Ranged: bow and a two-handed axe, no
    shield. Cavalry: lance + big round shield + two-handed mace, axe + big round shield.
  - Two-handed setups clear the shield slot (Item1): an AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn without item sets an empty element
    (AlternativeEquipmentEffect.Deserialize).
  - Sidearm (Item2) rule: spears and lances keep the culture's sidearm, since they fight poorly up close (the levy a
    raider axe, the men-at-arms a northern sword, the riders a two-handed maul). Axe setups and the two-handed axe
    clear it: their main weapon already is one.
  - A bad node makes the loader drop every later entry of this file silently; the CommanderBattle log lists the
    classes per culture when a mission opens.
  - Items only from Native's mpitems.xml (the only items multiplayer loads).
-->
